751		\leanok
752		\uses{def:generalized-pauli, def:subfield-trace}
753		All identities are verified on computational basis states. For the product
754		relations with $W = X$, shifting twice by $a'$ and $a$ equals shifting by
755		$a + a'$; with $W = Z$, the phases $\omega^{\tr(aj)}\omega^{\tr(a'j)}$
756		combine by $\F_q$-linearity of the trace, and the power relation follows by
757		iterating. For the scalar twisted commutation,
758		$\tau^X(a)\tau^Z(b)\ket{j} = \omega^{\tr(bj)}\ket{j + a}$, while
759		$\tau^Z(b)\tau^X(a)\ket{j} = \omega^{\tr(b(j+a))}\ket{j + a} =
760		\omega^{\tr(ab)}\,\omega^{\tr(bj)}\ket{j + a}$. The multi-qudit relation
761		follows by applying the scalar relation factor by factor and summing the
762		exponents, using $\tr(a \cdot b) = \sum_i \tr(a_i b_i)$. For $q = p$ the
763		trace is the identity map, which gives \eqref{eq:twisted-fp}.
764	\end{proof}
